{
  "$comment": "Cross-language conformance fixture for the request drafts an OpenAPI import builds (issue #865). Read by BOTH the engine gtest suite (openapi_drafts_test.cpp, via VAYU_ENGINE_SOURCE_DIR) and the app's vitest suite (app/src/services/openapi/spec-request-drafts.conformance.test.ts). A draft is not an identity - it is the request an import would build - and the spec sync diff compares a stored request against one, so a draft the two sides build differently is a field reported as changed for a document that did not change. Every case's `drafts` are keyed by 'METHOD path' rather than ordered, because the engine walks the document while readSpecOperations walks the collection tree it built (root requests, then tag folders) - two orders both sides agree about. Generated from the renderer's own parsers; regenerate by hand only with a matching engine change.",
